$ Shallow-water propagation over a submerged bar with the original LTA triads
$
$ TRIAD ITRIAD=11 is the LTA as it stood before release 41.01, and it is the
$ formulation the operational so-rp suite selects. It is not a spelling of
$ TRIAD LTA: ITRIAD = 11 drops the shoaling factor (FT = 0 in SWLTA) and takes
$ the group velocity from the local spectrum instead of the offshore one, and
$ the parser gives it different defaults as well (TRFAC 0.05 against 1.0,
$ CUTFR 2.5 against -1, DINT 0 against 60).
$
$ Before this deck no case under examples/ selected it -- triad_lta.swn claimed
$ to in its header while its command line reads TRIAD LTA, which is ITRIAD = 1,
$ and the coverage regex accepted either spelling for one formulation. So the
$ bounds-checked CI build never reached the ITRIAD = 11 arms of SWLTA.
$
$ Identical to triad_lta.swn apart from the triad command, so the two decks
$ isolate the difference between the two LTA generations.
PROJECT 'TRIADL11' '001'
SET CARTESIAN
MODE STATIONARY ONEDIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30.0 0.0 300 0 &
      SECTOR -10.0 10.0 20 0.10 2.0 31
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30 0 1.0 1.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 1 0 FREE

BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 0.06 2.0 0.0 2.0

GEN3 WESTH
OFF WINDGROWTH
OFF WCAPPING
OFF QUADRUPLET
TRIAD ITRIAD=11

POINTS 'GAUGES' 2.0 0.0 10.0 0.0 15.0 0.0 18.0 0.0 &
         25.0 0.0 30.0 0.0
TABLE 'GAUGES' HEADER 'triad_lta11.tbl' XP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 RTP REDTRIAD REDQUAD
SPECOUT 'GAUGES' SPEC1D ABS 'triad_lta11.spc'
TEST 1 0 POINTS XY 15.0 0.0 S1D 'triad_lta11_sources.spc'

COMPUTE
STOP
